<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch greens call off Schiphol blockade.</title>
<headline>Dutch greens call off Schiphol blockade.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch environmental lobby group Milieudefensie said on Friday it would not be holding its planned demonstration at Schiphol airport on Sunday after a ruling from a local magistrate.</p>
<p>The group had planned to disrupt flights for two hours in protest against the continued growth in air traffic. Around 500 activists were due to float aluminium-coated balloons and kites around the airport terrain.</p>
<p>Milieudefensie said activists would now move their protest on Sunday to inside the departure hall.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
